# 7. Inference object

The inference object represents one inferential move.

```yaml
inference:
  inference_id: INF-IIT-05

  from_claims:
    - CL-IIT-INTRINSIC-CAUSE
    - CL-IIT-IRREDUCIBILITY
    - CL-IIT-MAXIMALITY

  to_claim:
    CL-P05-003

  inference_form:
    identity_inference

  explicit_bridge:
    Intrinsic causal unity is identical with phenomenal unity.

  bridge_status:
    unsupported

  validity_status:
    invalid_without_bridge

  failure_description:
    The premises characterize intrinsic causal structure but do not
    independently establish phenomenal co-presence.

  countermodels:
    - CM-INTEGRATED-NONPHENOMENAL

  burden:
    Show why causal irreducibility constitutes rather than correlates
    with phenomenal unity.

  generated_branch:
    RB-P05-INTRINSICNESS
```

