# 27. Cross-edge dependencies

The ladder is sequential, but arguments may depend on non-adjacent pressures.

Example:

[
P_07
\rightarrow
P_03
]

because ownership can stabilize perspective.

[
P_08
\rightarrow
P_02
]

because agency can help constitute organisation.

[
P_05
\rightarrow
P_03
]

because co-presence may define the standpoint rather than follow from it.

Store these as:

```yaml
cross_dependency:
  dependency_id: XD-001
  source_pressure: P07
  target_pressure: P03
  relation:
    recursive_stabilisation
  claim:
    Recurrent affective ownership may help construct the operative perspective.
```

The pressure ladder is therefore a research order, not a commitment to simple linear causation.

