# 32. Contradiction engine

The graph should detect contradictions between promoted claims.

Example:

```yaml
contradiction:
  contradiction_id: CON-001

  claim_a:
    Phenomenal unity is an equivalence relation.

  claim_b:
    Phenomenal unity can be non-transitive.

  contradiction_type:
    direct

  resolution_required:
    - restrict_scope
    - downgrade_claim
    - split_concept
    - reject_one_claim
```

Many apparent contradictions will require scope distinctions.

Example:

[
\text{local phenomenal unity may be transitive}
]

while:

[
\text{layered unity may be non-transitive}.
