# 43. Quality tests

## Test 1 — Countermodel completeness

Every major inference must have at least one serious countermodel.

## Test 2 — Source locality

Every textual claim must point to a precise passage.

## Test 3 — Bridge exposure

Every nontrivial inference must state its bridge premise.

## Test 4 — Scope consistency

A claim about local cognition cannot silently become universal.

## Test 5 — Measurement discipline

Measured variables must remain distinct from inferred phenomenology.

## Test 6 — Terminological stability

Every technical term must reference a definition version.

## Test 7 — Checkpoint inheritance

A child checkpoint must state what it:

* retains;
* revises;
* rejects;
* adds.

## Test 8 — Frontier minimality

The residual frontier must be the smallest unresolved premise, not a broad topic.

